{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523215-question-about-few-gifts","id":1523215,"title":"Question about few gifts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-09-27T10:24:47-07:00","id":1523215,"title":"Question about few gifts","content":"There's some gift that need more detail than juste what's written<br /> <br /> Mother's touch: it heal the target, ok, but can it cure it from a bad disease? I mean disease like cancer and aids, poisons like cyanure... cause i'm planning to put an assamite against my player that will use quietus 2 against them, and i would like to know if a werewolf loosing 3 moint of stamina for a month can be cured with that gift<br /> <br /> Jam technology: the description tell it stop a certain complexity of technology, bit at difficulty 9 if it stop a blade to cut it wpuld logicammy stop a hammer to smash, stop an armor to protect and so on, at least if the ST allow it<br /> <br /> Hero stand: it tell that the character cannot move but how exactly? He cannot move from where he stand and stay still or does it mean he cannot leave from the area he activated the gift? And can you use the dice it give you with your soak and damage as these roll are physicall &quot;action&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 09-27-2023, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T12:09:32-07:00","id":1523227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523215-question-about-few-gifts#post1523215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's some gift that need more detail than juste what's written<br /> <br /> Mother's touch: it heal the target, ok, but can it cure it from a bad disease? I mean disease like cancer and aids, poisons like cyanure... cause i'm planning to put an assamite against my player that will use quietus 2 against them, and i would like to know if a werewolf loosing 3 moint of stamina for a month can be cured with that gift</div> </div> </div> </div>Mother's Touch heals damage, though you could rule it a kind of battle scar. That said, I don't know if you're going to find Kindred that can get four successes up on a Garou rolling their Crinos Stamina with potential bonuses for Resist Toxin vs the vampire's Willpower, so... good luck on that. Most diseases and toxins, incidentally, will tend to do jack-all to Garou and other shapeshifters with regeneration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Jam technology: the description tell it stop a certain complexity of technology, bit at difficulty 9 if it stop a blade to cut it wpuld logicammy stop a hammer to smash, stop an armor to protect and so on, at least if the ST allow it </div> </div> </div>Might as well. Difficulty 9 is hard to hit and won't be giving you much time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hero stand: it tell that the character cannot move but how exactly? He cannot move from where he stand and stay still or does it mean he cannot leave from the area he activated the gift? And can you use the dice it give you with your soak and damage as these roll are physicall &quot;action&quot;? </div> </div> </div>The user is rooted where they stand. That doesn't necessarily entail standing completely still. The bonus dice are probably meant for non-reflexive actions, but I guess you could apply them to damage and soak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T14:22:37-07:00","id":1523235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523215-question-about-few-gifts?p=1523227#post1523227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mother's Touch heals damage, though you could rule it a kind of battle scar. That said, I don't know if you're going to find Kindred that can get four successes up on a Garou rolling their Crinos Stamina with potential bonuses for Resist Toxin vs the vampire's Willpower, so... good luck on that. Most diseases and toxins, incidentally, will tend to do jack-all to Garou and other shapeshifters with regeneration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe not 4 success but even with one day (3 success) or one hour (2 success) it could be enough to kill a garou on a long fight or dangerous situation, none of my pc posess the &quot;Resist Toxin\u200b&quot; gift, the vampire have 10 willpower to activate the power and the most resistant pc has 8 stamina in crinos form. As it sill has a fair chance to weaken him for longer than a scene it would be usefull to know if mother touch can cure someone from vampire or wyrm poison.<br /> And by the way have i missed it or there's no line that tell Quietus 2 cannot be used more than once on a same target? Can an assamite use that power more than once on their ennemy to be sure to put them down?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 09-27-2023, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T14:43:47-07:00","id":1523237,"title":"","content":"Mother's Touch doesn't as written, cure diseases. WtA has a dearth of anti-disease and anti-toxin powers because they basically need to be supernaturally strong to matter anyway, and they want supernatural toxins to be some sort of threat. Keep in mind though, that the Garou have an extremely versatile toolkit in the forms of the Rite of Binding and the Rte of Spirit Awakening. If the Garou know they're facing something that likes using supernatural poisons and toxins, they can get temporary protection via those Rites.<br /> <br /> That said, if you're worried about your PCs.... maybe don't give the antagonists 10 Willpower?<br /> <br /> Also... these aren't games that are designed for crossover, how Quietus works against Garou is kinda up to you because there's lots of places where how vampire Disciplines and werewolf powers/Gifts aren't worded in compatible ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-28T01:04:24-07:00","id":1523262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523215-question-about-few-gifts?p=1523237#post1523237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mother's Touch doesn't as written, cure diseases. WtA has a dearth of anti-disease and anti-toxin powers because they basically need to be supernaturally strong to matter anyway, and they want supernatural toxins to be some sort of threat. Keep in mind though, that the Garou have an extremely versatile toolkit in the forms of the Rite of Binding and the Rte of Spirit Awakening. If the Garou know they're facing something that likes using supernatural poisons and toxins, they can get temporary protection via those Rites.</div> </div> </div> </div>So basically Mother's Touch will somehow &quot;reset&quot; the patient state, if aids gonna kill him the gift will regenerate him but not cure aids, like somekind of a supernatural treatment until a permanent cure is found. I already thought about talen, if one can heal 4 wound level then a talen that cure fatal disease would certainly be found, as for awakening a curing substance to permanently cure the patient.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523215-question-about-few-gifts?p=1523237#post1523237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, if you're worried about your PCs.... maybe don't give the antagonists 10 Willpower?</div> </div> </div> </div>That vampire is one of my main antagonist, i need him to be dangerous especially when facing something as dangerous for him as a werewolf pack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523215-question-about-few-gifts?p=1523237#post1523237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also... these aren't games that are designed for crossover, how Quietus works against Garou is kinda up to you because there's lots of places where how vampire Disciplines and werewolf powers/Gifts aren't worded in compatible ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not been a problem since then, i've just taken what's useful for my game and leave the rest.<br /> <br /> So mother touch is only about healing wound and damage from poison and illness, it cannot erase them from the organism so a better (spiritual) treatment is necessary to cure them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 09-28-2023, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-29T12:53:21-07:00","id":1523320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523215-question-about-few-gifts?p=1523235#post1523235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe not 4 success but even with one day (3 success) or one hour (2 success) it could be enough to kill a garou on a long fight or dangerous situation, none of my pc posess the &quot;Resist Toxin\u200b&quot; gift, the vampire have 10 willpower to activate the power and the most resistant pc has 8 stamina in crinos form. As it sill has a fair chance to weaken him for longer than a scene it would be usefull to know if mother touch can cure someone from vampire or wyrm poison.<br /> And by the way have i missed it or there's no line that tell Quietus 2 cannot be used more than once on a same target? Can an assamite use that power more than once on their ennemy to be sure to put them down?</div> </div> </div> </div>Statistically speaking, you're going to be getting just one success over the Stamina 8 guy 50% of the time. As for multiple times, you're kind of skating on thin ice just to use it once on account of being around Garou, which is a very risky proposition on account of the genre difference (personal horror types don't want to get splattered, but if you deal with the Garou that's all part of the risk). Personally, I'd just have it reset the duration if it scores more successes rather than try to keep track of cumulative successes, especially if it happens over time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-29T15:27:51-07:00","id":1523329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523215-question-about-few-gifts?p=1523320#post1523320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Statistically speaking, you're going to be getting just one success over the Stamina 8 guy 50% of the time. As for multiple times, you're kind of skating on thin ice just to use it once on account of being around Garou, which is a very risky proposition on account of the genre difference (personal horror types don't want to get splattered, but if you deal with the Garou that's all part of the risk). Personally, I'd just have it reset the duration if it scores more successes rather than try to keep track of cumulative successes, especially if it happens over time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was not thinking about the duration of the poison but cumulating the destruction of stamina, let's say the vampire score 2 success, the poison will last for an hour, but with his 4 dots in stamina he could invest 4 blood point and destroy 4 dots of the werewolf stamina four an entire hour. That mean a huge weakness to the big bad wolf, and the vampire will rely on his speed and intelligence to strike and flee, letting his allies deliver the coup de grace with their rifles. And if the vampire can use quietus 2 again to destroy more of the werewolf stamina it will be even more dangerous","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-29T16:46:41-07:00","id":1523330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523215-question-about-few-gifts?p=1523329#post1523329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was not thinking about the duration of the poison but cumulating the destruction of stamina, let's say the vampire score 2 success, the poison will last for an hour, but with his 4 dots in stamina he could invest 4 blood point and destroy 4 dots of the werewolf stamina four an entire hour. That mean a huge weakness to the big bad wolf, and the vampire will rely on his speed and intelligence to strike and flee, letting his allies deliver the coup de grace with their rifles. And if the vampire can use quietus 2 again to destroy more of the werewolf stamina it will be even more dangerous</div> </div> </div> </div>Something that's oft-overlooked is that if you try to sneak up on super wolves with guns is that they're going to smell the gunpowder and grease, possibly even when the wind is blowing in the other direction (Heightened Senses!).<br /> <br /> Just go with one per for Q2. Unless you want the vampire to have to go feed in the middle of combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-29T17:41:52-07:00","id":1523331,"title":"","content":"Unless it is the whole purpose, the werewolf is concentrate on the people shooting at him and the vampire strike by surprise from behind with Q2 to weaken the beast, leaving it more vulnerable to the attack. Using the chaos of the fight for surprise attack is a good strategy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-30T09:12:20-07:00","id":1523358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523215-question-about-few-gifts?p=1523331#post1523331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless it is the whole purpose, the werewolf is concentrate on the people shooting at him and the vampire strike by surprise from behind with Q2 to weaken the beast, leaving it more vulnerable to the attack. Using the chaos of the fight for surprise attack is a good strategy</div> </div> </div> </div>No, like, the entire ambush is full of things that are fairly obvious to wolf senses, especially after being ramped up. The players should have a chance to see it coming a mile away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-03T14:36:23-07:00","id":1535113,"title":"","content":"Re-opening the thread about the Rank 5 gift Thousand Forms. I want to introduce a traitor elder ragabash with it and in case of battle i need some detail:<br /> <br /> -Is there any stat bonus/malus to physical attribute when used to take the form of a bear, eagle, cat, lion and so on?<br /> <br /> -You cannot take the form of a wyrm creature, only mythical beast, but what about cinema one? You could say that it depend on what the st decide but if you can take the form of the griffin wich is an invented creature why would you not be able to take the form of a xenomorph wich also is an invented creature? Or gremlins? Or anything like that? (And the st would need to sort these creatures to find out if they were Wyrm or not in addition)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-03T15:07:20-07:00","id":1535114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523215-question-about-few-gifts?p=1535113#post1535113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re-opening the thread about the Rank 5 gift Thousand Forms. I want to introduce a traitor elder ragabash with it and in case of battle i need some detail:<br /> <br /> -Is there any stat bonus/malus to physical attribute when used to take the form of a bear, eagle, cat, lion and so on?<br /> <br /> -You cannot take the form of a wyrm creature, only mythical beast, but what about cinema one? You could say that it depend on what the st decide but if you can take the form of the griffin wich is an invented creature why would you not be able to take the form of a xenomorph wich also is an invented creature? Or gremlins? Or anything like that? (And the st would need to sort these creatures to find out if they were Wyrm or not in addition)</div> </div> </div> </div>You can either use arbitrary stats found in various WoD games or the forms for a given Fera's form. As for invented or mythic creatures, the cutoff is probably such that you could consult the Bygone Bestiary but not random entries from B.J. Zanzibar's fan-made material compilation site. So, yes for griffins, hippogrifs, and dragons, but not for xenomorphs, yautja, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-03T16:27:14-07:00","id":1535115,"title":"","content":"Myth and recent cultural inventions just aren't the same thing. Gremlins is a relatively new concept that's on the cusp of myth and recent invention, but it's also a direct modification of goblin myths mixed with changing technology. The mogwai from the film Gremlins don't really draw from aviation gremlins, goblins, or Chinese mogwai in any meaningful sense. They're more like imps but called gremlins to remove the religious implication of &quot;imp&quot; to a western audience..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-03T17:23:19-07:00","id":1535119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523215-question-about-few-gifts?p=1535114#post1535114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, yes for griffins, hippogrifs, and dragons, but not for xenomorphs, yautja, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Myth and recent cultural inventions just aren't the same thing</div> </div> </div> </div>So i assume the reason is that the mythical beast are part of legends once believed real while actual cinema creature are entertainment creature no one would believe real?<br /> <br /> As it isn't specified in the w20 gift description (previous version i've found either), it's hard to know how the gift is supposed to work with non existing beast and stats modification","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-04T00:47:39-07:00","id":1535133,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that in the WoD most legendary/mythical creatures were actually real in-universe. Unicorns, griffins, dragons, etc. either are still around hidden from human eyes, or were once living creatures that coexisted with the rest of the world until the end of the Mythic Age pushed more and more of them into the Umbra.<br /> <br /> For us, in the real world, a mythical creature from tales from 5,000 years ago, and a made up movie monster from the last few years might be equally imaginary. For Garou in the WoD, it's very likely the older one is seen as a real thing that either can be found to this day to supernaturals such as themselves, or were until humanity spreading the Weaver around killed them off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-04T02:02:37-07:00","id":1535135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523215-question-about-few-gifts?p=1535133#post1535133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep in mind that in the WoD most legendary/mythical creatures were actually real in-universe. Unicorns, griffins, dragons, etc. either are still around hidden from human eyes, or were once living creatures that coexisted with the rest of the world until the end of the Mythic Age pushed more and more of them into the Umbra.<br /> <br /> For us, in the real world, a mythical creature from tales from 5,000 years ago, and a made up movie monster from the last few years might be equally imaginary. For Garou in the WoD, it's very likely the older one is seen as a real thing that either can be found to this day to supernaturals such as themselves, or were until humanity spreading the Weaver around killed them off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, didn't know that they were real spirits/being in the past, that explain how this gift work, thanks<br /> <br /> A gift that let you turn into one of the cinema creature would be cool though, if it let you choose only one and you create it's stat and ability with the st","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 05-04-2024, 05:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-04T03:43:17-07:00","id":1535137,"title":"","content":"Hey wait a minutes when it come to mythical creature we find vampires, grim reaper, undeads and many more. Ok vampire considering the wod would be wyrm creature, but the grim reaper? tough one","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-04T10:23:56-07:00","id":1535144,"title":"","content":"There isn't a specific &quot;grim reaper&quot; in the WoD. The closest thing are the Ferrymen, who are &quot;just&quot; really powerful Wraiths. Though a few Demons might claim that too (since some of them think Charon the founder of the Ferrymen was actually one of them).<br /> <br /> Being associated with death, they're certainly going to be a bit Wyrm-y to Garou senses, but like most Wraiths their balance of traits is going to matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-04T16:17:40-07:00","id":1535153,"title":"","content":"The ST should really stick to classical mythologic beast, and not demon or concept incarnation like grim reaper in that case. Ghost are not of the wyrm by nature but as they're not specific entity i doubt the gift allow the pc to turn into one. Hard to define a line when you look mythology in detail when you see the number of creature there is in different cultures","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-04T19:47:34-07:00","id":1535154,"title":"","content":"The Grim Reaper would be considered to be an Epiphling of Death. It's a spirit that embodies the concept of death. It wouldn't be a mythical beast per that Gift. At least that is how I would run it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-05T09:17:50-07:00","id":1535174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523215-question-about-few-gifts?p=1535154#post1535154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Grim Reaper would be considered to be an Epiphling of Death. It's a spirit that embodies the concept of death. It wouldn't be a mythical beast per that Gift. At least that is how I would run it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, you're right<br /> Anyway i think i will skip the mythical beast part, some of my friend told me about some of other folklore and culture and let's say that it allow way too many things. They told me about some who could raise dead, make the sun rise anytime, possess mortal... If my friend's Ragabash pc achieve rank 5 one day and obtain it i don't know with what he could come and i wouldn't even know how to handle such ability, even if it's me controling the npc using it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}